{"astp_version": "0.1.0", "event_type": "turn", "session": {"id": "s-777184608880", "start_time": "2026-09-22T10:39:43.119Z", "user_id": "u-claims-0417", "tenant_id": "thornfield-mutual", "client_app": "claims-copilot", "agent_id": "astp-lab-agent-1", "config_version": "0.2.0"}, "turn": {"index": 0, "timestamp": "2026-09-22T10:39:51.015Z", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5", "model_version": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "tokens_in": 13375, "tokens_out": 102, "latency": 7.872, "finish_reason": "tool_use"}, "content": {"prompt_text": "What is the fraud referral procedure, and at what point does a claim have to be referred?", "prompt_hash": "sha256:c41eae1b6df85dd983a6d0ffba0a08a6dfe3f2fbe0e42bfdec85cc5c09acf816", "response_text": "I'll search for information about Thornfield Mutual's fraud referral procedure.", "response_hash": "sha256:d79af58de77baaca7b12de1998b1c0bbb85bd3da8278a866d21ccf22ceeca889", "system_prompt_version": "sp-0.2.0", "redaction_applied": false}, "control": {"canary_triggered": false, "policy_version": "0.1.0", "block_reason": null}}
{"astp_version": "0.1.0", "event_type": "turn", "session": {"id": "s-777184608880", "start_time": "2026-09-22T10:39:43.119Z", "user_id": "u-claims-0417", "tenant_id": "thornfield-mutual", "client_app": "claims-copilot", "agent_id": "astp-lab-agent-1", "config_version": "0.2.0"}, "turn": {"index": 1, "timestamp": "2026-09-22T10:39:51.275Z", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5", "model_version": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "tokens_in": 14611, "tokens_out": 369, "latency": 0.259, "finish_reason": "end_turn"}, "content": {"prompt_text": "What is the fraud referral procedure, and at what point does a claim have to be referred?", "prompt_hash": "sha256:c41eae1b6df85dd983a6d0ffba0a08a6dfe3f2fbe0e42bfdec85cc5c09acf816", "response_text": "Based on the fraud referral procedure, here's what you need to know:\n\n## When to refer\n\n**Referral is warranted where two or more of the following indicators are present, or where any one of them is strongly present:**\n\n- The policy was taken out or increased within thirty days of the incident\n- The incident happened at an unusual hour with no independent witness\n- Documents supplied are copies where originals would be expected, or carry inconsistent dates, fonts or reference numbers\n- The claimant is unusually familiar with policy wording or claims process\n- The same address, bank account or telephone number appears on unconnected claims\n- Injuries reported do not match the damage to the vehicle or property\n- The claimant presses for a quick cash settlement and declines an inspection\n- Receipts are sequential, from a single supplier, and round numbered\n\n## The procedure\n\nWhen you spot these indicators, you should:\n\n1. **Raise a referral on the counter fraud queue** — do not investigate yourself. That decision belongs to the counter fraud team.\n2. **Carry on handling the claim normally**\n3. **Do not tell the claimant** a referral has been made\n4. **Do not mention the referral or reasons for it** in any correspondence to the claimant\n\n## What happens after referral\n\nThe counter fraud team acknowledges within two working days and gives one of three outcomes: no further action, monitor, or investigate. If they decide to investigate, all contact with the claimant passes to them and you stop corresponding. Payments cannot be made without written agreement from the counter fraud lead.\n\n([prc-fraud-002](prc-fraud-002))", "response_hash": "sha256:90207148c0499366330ccdc38a937baa3686d32e22957cd3e372555b8260f807", "system_prompt_version": "sp-0.2.0", "redaction_applied": false}, "control": {"canary_triggered": false, "policy_version": "0.1.0", "block_reason": null}}
